      "id": 167,
      "start": 377.64,
      "end": 378.49,
      "en": "Really, it's no problem.",
      "zh": "真的，没问题。"
    },
    {
      "id": 168,
      "start": 379.68,
      "end": 380.93,
      "en": "Just hang on there a sec.",
      "zh": "请稍等一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 169,
      "start": 382.28,
      "end": 386.4,
      "en": "Can I get a price check on Funtime's ribbed condoms, please?",
      "zh": "请帮我查一下 Funtime 螺纹避孕套的价格好吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 170,
      "start": 393.02,
      "end": 400.34,
      "en": "Okay, so now it's time for us to take a look at some of the phrases that we saw in this dialogue in Putting It Together.",
      "zh": "好的，现在是时候在综合运用环节看看这段对话里的一些短语了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 171,
      "start": 402.86,
      "end": 403.6,
      "en": "Putting It Together.",
      "zh": "综合运用。"
    },
    {
      "id": 172,
      "start": 405.64,
      "end": 410.64,
      "en": "We're going to look at two phrases here and we're going to see how we can use them in different situations.",
      "zh": "我们将在这里查看两个短语，我们将看看如何在不同的情况下使用它们。"
    },
    {
      "id": 173,
      "start": 411.28,
      "end": 415.94,
      "en": "The pharmacist warned, be sure not to take it on an empty stomach.",
      "zh": "药剂师警告，一定不要空腹服用。"
    },
    {
      "id": 174,
      "start": 416.24,
      "end": 418.36,
      "en": "Okay, so be sure not to.",
      "zh": "好的，所以一定不要。"
    },
    {
      "id": 175,
      "start": 418.6,
      "end": 419.76,
      "en": "Be sure not to.",
      "zh": "一定不要。"
    },
    {
      "id": 176,
      "start": 420.38,
      "end": 421.84,
      "en": "What does he mean by this?",
      "zh": "他这是什么意思？"
    },
    {
      "id": 177,
      "start": 422.14,
      "end": 423.48,
      "en": "He just means don't do this.",
      "zh": "他只是说不要这样做。"
    },
    {
      "id": 178,
      "start": 423.9,
      "end": 424.12,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 179,
      "start": 424.92,
      "end": 427.04,
      "en": "So don't take the medicine without eating.",
      "zh": "所以不要不吃就吃药。"
    },
    {
      "id": 180,
      "start": 427.04,
      "end": 428.48,
      "en": "We can mix it up a little bit.",
      "zh": "我们可以稍微变换一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 181,
      "start": 428.62,
      "end": 432.52,
      "en": "Why don't we listen to some examples of how we can use this in different situations.",
      "zh": "我们为什么不听一些我们如何在不同情况下使用它的例子。"
    },
    {
      "id": 182,
      "start": 434.8,
      "end": 438.02,
      "en": "Example one.",
      "zh": "例句一。"
    },
    {
      "id": 183,
      "start": 438.02,
      "end": 440.31,
      "en": "Be sure not to leave your bike outside or it will be stolen.",
      "zh": "一定不要把你的自行车放在外面，否则它会被偷走。"
    },
    {
      "id": 184,
      "start": 444.32,
      "end": 447.12,
      "en": "Example two.",
      "zh": "例句二。"
    },
    {
      "id": 185,
      "start": 447.12,
      "end": 448.27,
      "en": "Be sure not to forget your umbrella.",
      "zh": "一定不要忘记你的雨伞。"
    },
    {
      "id": 186,
      "start": 448.84,
      "end": 449.47,
      "en": "It's raining today.",
      "zh": "今天下雨了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 187,
      "start": 453.28,
      "end": 456.28,
      "en": "Example three.",
      "zh": "例句三。"
    },
    {
      "id": 188,
      "start": 456.28,
      "end": 459.31,
      "en": "I told him to be sure not to do anything stupid, but he did.",
      "zh": "我告诉他一定不要做任何愚蠢的事情，但他做到了。"
    },
    {
      "id": 189,
      "start": 463.72,
      "end": 468.37,
      "en": "So Marco, why should we say be sure not to instead of don't?",
      "zh": "Marco，为什么我们要说 be sure not to，而不是直接说 don't 呢？"
    },
    {
      "id": 190,
      "start": 468.76,
      "end": 471.29,
      "en": "I think don't sounds more like an order.",
      "zh": "我觉得 don't 听起来更像命令。"
    },
    {
      "id": 191,
      "start": 471.64,
      "end": 472.64,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 192,
      "start": 472.64,
      "end": 473.64,
      "en": "Very direct.",
      "zh": "很直接。"
    },
    {
      "id": 193,
      "start": 473.64,
      "end": 476.85,
      "en": "Maybe be sure not to is a little bit softer, a little bit more friendly.",
      "zh": "也许 be sure not to 语气更柔和一点，也更友好一点。"
    },
    {
      "id": 194,
      "start": 477.42,
      "end": 478.37,
      "en": "So be sure not to.",
      "zh": "所以一定不要。"
    },
    {
      "id": 195,
      "start": 478.91,
      "end": 480.51,
      "en": "Now for our last phrase.",
      "zh": "现在是我们的最后一句话。"
    },
    {
      "id": 196,
      "start": 480.95,
      "end": 486.99,
      "en": "So the pharmacist in the end wanted to check for the price and he said, just hang on there a sec.",
      "zh": "所以药剂师最终想检查价格，他说，等一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 197,
      "start": 487.67,
      "end": 488.41,
      "en": "So that's interesting.",
      "zh": "所以这很有趣。"
    },
    {
      "id": 198,
      "start": 489.07,
      "end": 489.57,
      "en": "Hang on.",
      "zh": "等一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 199,
      "start": 490.29,
      "end": 490.65,
      "en": "Hang on.",
      "zh": "等一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 200,
      "start": 491.28,
      "end": 492.28,
      "en": "Hang on.",
      "zh": "等一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 201,
      "start": 492.28,
      "end": 492.65,
      "en": "Well, hang on.",
      "zh": "嗯，等一下。"
    },
    {
      "id": 202,
      "start": 493.28,
      "end": 494.17,
      "en": "What does he mean by hang on?",
      "zh": "他说的是什么意思？"
    },
